(11897,'Selecting scopes here will be set as default when authorizing (so no need to specify the scope parameter on the token request), also the selection of scopes will limit the allowed scopes on the consumer/client.','','11.2.2'),
(11898,'The absolute URIs to validate against.','','11.2.2'),
(11899,'The number of seconds that the access token will be valid.','','11.2.2'),
(11900,'The number of seconds that the refresh token will be valid.','','11.2.2'),
(11901,'When no specific user is authenticated Drupal will use this user as the author of all the actions made.','','11.2.2'),
(11902,'A boolean indicating whether the client uses @pkce (e.g., a native client or SPA)','','11.2.2'),
(11903,'This will cause the authorization form to be skipped.','','11.2.2'),
(11904,'When enabled, if previous authorization request with the same scopes got approved, authorization will be automatically accepted.','','11.2.2'),
(11905,'Generate random Client ID','','11.2.2'),
(11906,'New Secret','','11.2.2'),
(11907,'Use this field to create a hash of the secret key. This module will never store your consumer key, only a hash of it.','','11.2.2'),
(11908,'Authorization Code settings','','11.2.2'),
(11909,'Client Credentials settings','','11.2.2'),
(11910,'Refresh Token settings','','11.2.2'),
(11911,'Check the <a href=\"@href\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Simple OAuth guide</a> for OpenID Connect to learn how to customize the user claims for OpenID Connect.','','11.2.2'),
(11912,'Disable OpenID Connect','','11.2.2'),
(11913,'Disable OpenID Connect if you have a conflicting custom or contributed implementation of OpenID Connect in your site.','','11.2.2'),
(11914,'Available claims','','11.2.2'),
(11915,'Claims are defined and managed in the service container. They are only listed here for reference. Please see the documentation above for more information.','','11.2.2'),
(11916,'Add Scope','','11.2.2'),
(11917,'A unique name for this scope. It must only contain lowercase letters, numbers, underscores, and colons.','','11.2.2'),
(11918,'Description of the scope.','','11.2.2'),
(11919,'Description for %grant_type','','11.2.2'),
(11920,'Enable the scope for specific grant types and optionally give a specific scope description per grant type.','','11.2.2'),
(11921,'Umbrella','','11.2.2'),
(11922,'An umbrella scope groups multiple scopes.','','11.2.2'),
(11923,'If a client requests the parent scope it also has any children scopes.','','11.2.2'),
(11924,'Save scope','','11.2.2'),
(11925,'Add scope','','11.2.2'),
(11926,'Note: If none of the selected menus contain an item for a given page, Drupal will look in the \'Navigation\' menu by default, even if it is \'disabled\' here.','','11.2.2'),
(11927,'Enable the Menu Breadcrumb module','','11.2.2'),
(11928,'Use menu the page belongs to, or the page for the taxonomy of which it is a member, for the breadcrumb. If unset, no breadcrumbs are generated or cached by this module and all settings below are ignored.','','11.2.2'),
(11929,'Disable for admin pages','','11.2.2'),
(11930,'Do not build menu-based breadcrumbs for admin pages.','','11.2.2'),
(11931,'Append current page to breadcrumb','','11.2.2'),
(11932,'If current page is on a menu, include it in the breadcrumb trail.','','11.2.2'),
(11933,'Show current page as link','','11.2.2'),
(11934,'Set TRUE if the current page in the breadcrumb trail should be a link (otherwise it will be plain text).','','11.2.2'),
(11935,'Stop on the first matching','','11.2.2'),
(11936,'End the breadcrumb trail when the first matching found in the menu.','','11.2.2'),
(11937,'Attach taxonomy member page to breadcrumb','','11.2.2'),
(11938,'This option affects breadcrumb display when the current page is a member of a taxonomy whose term is on a menu with \"Taxonomy Attachment\" selected, when it \"attaches\" to the menu-based breadcrumbs of that taxonomy term. In this case that term\'s menu title will show as a link regardless of the \"current page\" options above. Set this option TRUE to also show the current (\"attached\") <i>page</i> title as the final breadcrumb.','','11.2.2'),
(11939,'Show attached current page as link','','11.2.2'),
(11940,'Set TRUE to show the attached final breadcrumb as a link (otherwise it will be plain text).','','11.2.2'),
(11941,'Remove \"Home\" link','','11.2.2'),
(11942,'Regardless of option settings, this module always checks if the first breadcrumb is also the &lt;front&gt; page. Without this option set, it will always replace the link for that node- or view- based path of the &lt;front&gt; page (e.g., /node/1 or /node) with a link to the site home. Set this option TRUE to <i>delete</i> the &lt;front&gt; breadcrumb rather than replacing it.','','11.2.2'),
(11943,'Add \"Home\" link','','11.2.2'),
(11944,'If TRUE will add a link to the &lt;front&gt; page if it doesn\'t already begin the breadcrumb trail: ensuring that the first breadcrumb of every page is the site home. If both \"add\" and \"remove\" are set, when displaying the &lt;front&gt; page and its menu children the \"remove\" option will take precedence.','','11.2.2'),
(11945,'Use \"Home\" as title','','11.2.2'),
(11946,'Uses the site name from the configuration settings: if this option is not set, a translated value for \"Home\" will be used.','','11.2.2'),
(11947,'Use title menu parent','','11.2.2'),
(11948,'Home title','','11.2.2'),
(11949,'Exclude menu items with empty URLs','','11.2.2'),
(11950,'If TRUE, menu items whose Link fields resolves to an empty string (like in the case \"&lt;none&gt;\" was used) will not be included in the breadcrumb trail.','','11.2.2'),
(11951,'Exclude disabled menu items','','11.2.2'),
(11952,'If TRUE, menu items that are disabled will not be included in the breadcrumb trail.','','11.2.2'),
(11953,'Derive MenuActiveTrail from RouteMatch','','11.2.2'),
(11954,'If FALSE, the injected @menu.active_trail service will be used. If you have a multilingual site with unusually large menus, see <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/menu_breadcrumb/issues/3083028\">issue 3083028</a>.','','11.2.2'),
(11955,'Taxonomy Attachment','','11.2.2'),
(11956,'Language Handling','','11.2.2'),
(11957,'<b>Order of operation:</b> The breadcrumb will be generated from the first match it finds: \"Enabled\" to look for the current item on the menu, then \"Taxonomy Attachment\" to look for its taxonomy term. Re-order the list to change the priority of each menu.<br><b>Language Handling:</b> If set, skip this menu when the defined menu language does not match the current content language: recommended setting when you use a separate menu per language. This has no effect on taxonomy attachment.','','11.2.2'),
